note: "Two T2 write-backs were considered; one landed and one is deliberately held. LANDED: DEC-30, which the epic's own distillation plan reserved ('a new decision record — why the app's one text input and one state dot are registry entries rather than screen-local'), plus its index row. HELD: the rulebook's chromatic-meanings row (StatusDot as a second owner of ok/warn, and ink-mute's first entry as the not-yet-known channel). It is argued in full in DEC-30 and it belongs in docs/design-rules/, but the rulebook is FROZEN INPUT for a design run and grows at distillation per DEC-14 — and four screen runs (W3/W5/W7/W9) are still to pin it. Moving it mid-epic would change a substrate they read. Carried to W11, where the epic's distillation plan already reserves the row. NOT MOVED, and stated rather than assumed: docs/use-cases/web-ui.html. No observable contract moved — the three components have no call site, so every screen renders exactly what it rendered before; UC-4's and UC-ONBOARD's wording is W4's and W10's to move if their builds move it. No T1 edit: the flow, rulebook and gate are inputs to this epic, and nothing this WU found argues the method is wrong — DEC-28 and DEC-29 had already fixed the one edge it probed, before it ran."
